\title{MultiOmicsBridge: Integrative Multi-Omics Analysis of Host
Transcriptomics and Gut Microbiome Data}
\description{
MultiOmicsBridge provides an end-to-end, reproducible computational
framework for integrative analysis of paired host transcriptomics
(bulk RNA-seq) and gut microbiome (16S rRNA or shotgun metagenomics)
data. The package bridges two complementary biological data layers that,
when analyzed together, reveal insights neither can provide alone.
}
\section{The problem this package solves}{

No single Bioconductor package provides all four critical capabilities
for host-microbiome integration in a unified, microbiome-aware workflow:
\enumerate{
  \item Proper normalization for \strong{compositional microbiome data}
    alongside RNA-seq count data.
  \item \strong{Joint dimensionality reduction} identifying shared
    variation patterns between the two data layers.
  \item \strong{Multi-omics biomarker selection} identifying which host
    genes and which microbial taxa jointly predict disease status.
  \item An \strong{integrated diagnostic classifier} demonstrating
    the added value of combining both data types over either alone.
}
MultiOmicsBridge provides all four in a single, opinionated pipeline.
}

\section{Five analysis modules}{

\describe{
  \item{Module 1 — Data Harmonization}{
    \code{\link{loadHostData}}, \code{\link{loadMicrobiomeData}},
    \code{\link{matchSamples}}: Import, normalize, and match paired
    omics data into a \code{MultiAssayExperiment}.}
  \item{Module 2 — Joint Dimensionality Reduction}{
    \code{\link{jointDimReduction}}: Sparse multi-block PLS-DA
    (DIABLO) identifying correlated features across data blocks.}
  \item{Module 3 — Biomarker Discovery}{
    \code{\link{biomarkerDiscovery}}: Sparse feature loadings and
    cross-omics correlation networks for multi-omics biomarker ranking.}
  \item{Module 4 — Diagnostic Classification}{
    \code{\link{diagnosticClassifier}}: Host-only, microbiome-only,
    and joint Random Forest classifiers with nested cross-validation.}
  \item{Module 5 — Visualization and Reporting}{
    \code{\link{plotIntegration}}, \code{\link{plotBiomarkerNetwork}},
    \code{\link{plotClassifierComparison}}, \code{\link{plotSankey}},
    \code{\link{generateReport}}.}
}
}

